BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Stanford University Libraries] What's New & Cool About Internatio
 nal Government Data
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T120000
DTSTAMP:20261119T211238Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-54499448544810-54499448544811@local-events
DESCRIPTION:With the launch of the United Nations System Data Commons last
  month\, semantic search has arrived to international government data. How
  is semantic search enabled for data\, and which organizations use it?\n\n
 We will explore generative artificial intelligence's role in international
  government data\, with a focus on the SDMX metadata standard\, OECD's "AI
  for data\, data for AI" initiative\, an IMF paper entitled "StatGPT"\, an
 d practical advice on using AI with this valuable data source.\n\nFeel fre
 e to\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-11-19 13:12 PST
LOCATION:Green Library\, Bing Wing
END:VEVENT
