SUMMARY:[History Department / Stanford Humanities Center] Galicia's Promis
 ed City with Oskar Czendze
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T133000
DTSTAMP:20261119T211238Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53950377018749-53950377018750@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Between 1890 and 1914\, tens of thousands of Jews from Galicia
 —the easternmost crownland of the Habsburg Empire—made New York City t
 heir new home. Yet their distinct experience has often been overshadowed b
 y national narratives centered on migration from the Russian Empire. Oskar
  Czendze (University of Toronto) will explores how Galician Jews carried f
 orms of regional and supranational belonging shaped in East Central Europe
  into New York. \n\nWhen: Thursday | Nov 19 | 12:00pm  \n\nWhere: Bldg. 20
 0 |\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1euIgnTpdat
 J3oa1vsQCf_V0GapwEdC6A-0gqpPE_M68/edit\nLast synced: 2026-11-19 13:12 PST
LOCATION:Building 200\, History Corner
URL:https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1euIgnTpdatJ3oa1vsQCf_V0GapwEdC6A-0gqp
 PE_M68/edit
END:VEVENT
