BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[The Europe Center] Jannis Panagiotidis- Racism against East Europ
 eans in Germany: History and Present
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T130000
DTSTAMP:20261119T211238Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-54037411906317-54037411908366@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Racism against East Europeans constitutes a major gap in racis
 m research and anti-racism debates. Yet there is a long tradition of treat
 ing the region and its inhabitants as inferior\, with devastating conseque
 nces throughout history. This book is the first comprehensive study of rac
 ism in the entangled histories of Germany and Eastern Europe—a racism th
 at is not based on skin color and affects people despite their mostly phen
 otypical whiteness. Embedded in colonial imaginations of Eastern Europe\n
 \nAges: All ages\nSource: https://tec.fsi.stanford.edu/events/panagiotidis
 \nLast synced: 2026-11-19 13:12 PST
LOCATION:Encina Hall
URL:https://tec.fsi.stanford.edu/events/panagiotidis
END:VEVENT
